# Production build directories
build/

# Database files. Deliberately a pattern, not four literal filenames: spelling
# the library's name out here means that renaming the file — for any reason —
# silently un-ignores it, and it holds every project and every private note.
# A pattern keeps it ignored whatever it is called.
server/*.db
server/*.db-journal
server/*.db-shm
server/*.db-wal

# What the desktop launcher leaves beside the library: the app window's own
# Chromium profile, the log, the marker for the Start Menu shortcut. All three
# go in the data directory, which is outside the tree for every real install —
# but a checkout started without one falls back to the historical layout and
# drops them in `server/`, where the profile alone reached 449 MB in four
# minutes and `git status` offered the whole of it.
server/browser-profile/
server/logs/
server/start-menu-shortcut.*

# Pre-upgrade snapshots. `database.js` copies the library before any release
# migrates it (once per version change, three most recent kept) — see
# CHANGELOG.md. These are full copies of a personal library, tens or hundreds of
# MB each, and without this line `git status` offers to commit one.
*.db.pre-*.bak
# Any other copy of the library, however it was named. The pattern above only
# matched the snapshots database.js writes itself; a backup taken by hand or by
# a tool (`<library>.db.bak-<stamp>`) sailed past it and sat in `git status` at
# 55 MB apiece, one `git add -A` away from a published repo.
*.db.bak*

# Vault — user-uploaded original files (content-addressed blob store)
server/vault/

# Local HTTPS certificates (mkcert) — never commit private keys
.certs/


# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Scratch: probes, harness runs, dry-run DBs (harnesses that ship live in tools/)
temp/

# Harness bundles are generated by esbuild on each run
tools/*/bundle.cjs

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/

# Desktop packages built by tools/build-desktop.mjs
release/

# Vite writes one of these beside vite.config.ts while loading the config and
# usually, but not always, deletes it again — a killed dev server leaves a
# zero-byte file in the repo root.
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*.mjs

# Local editor and assistant configuration, by PATTERN rather than by name:
# which tools someone builds with is not the repository's business, and a
# pattern also covers whatever dot-directory lands here next. `.github/` and
# `.githooks/` are the project's own, so they are named back in — the hook in
# there is what `npm run hooks` installs, and a pattern that swallowed it would
# publish a repository whose own setup step points at nothing.
/.*/
!/.github/
!/.githooks/
